Ticket **#4471** combines reports from two different causes. Split the work by cause, not by
the subject text used to merge the reports.

The export contains overlapping pages. The table deduplicates by report ID, so each report is
counted once.

## Cause breakdown

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Parser: shared code reads month first

The tenant directory uses day-first locales, while the shared parser reads dates month first.
For example, report `R-41200` says a 7 April reminder went out on 4 July. This is the cause
assigned to the majority of reports in #4471. Track it in [issue #1](https://github.com/olekihnatowicz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

## Hint: booking-v3 shows the wrong order

The `booking-v3` form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the affected tenants use day-first locales
and the form reads dates in the tenant's order. These reports come from form submissions for
`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, and `pale.harbour`. For example, `R-41230` says a client came
on 1 June instead of 6 January. Track it in [issue #2](https://github.com/olekihnatowicz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

Use the tenant configuration and intake channel to separate these causes. `meta.intakeTag` is
only an intake guess, and matching subjects hid both causes in #4471.

<Callout kind="warn">
  The desk notes flag some reports as one-day moves. The supplied cause model leaves them in
  the parser group by tenant and channel; keep that note visible, but do not count it as a
  separate cause without evidence of a separate root cause.
</Callout>

Issue #1 covers the parser cause; issue #2 covers the hint cause. Each issue uses the unique
report count shown above.

